	{
		"The Cards",
		"Blox Cards is a game that may seem very confusing to you at first, but don't worry! We'll go over what everything means! Firstly, there's three different types of cards. Action cards (Black cards), Arena cards (Blue cards), and fighters (Any other color). All cards in the game have a trait, a cost, and a rarity. A trait, is what color a card belongs to. This is found out by looking at the background of a card, and seeing what color it is. There are 5 traits in the game. White, Red, Blue, Yellow, and Green. This may not seem important at the moment, but later in the tutorial, when icons are explained, you'll see why it's one of the most vital aspects in the game. Next up is a card's rarity. This is shown in the top right of the card. There are 5 different rarities in the game. Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, and Legendary. Rarities have a meaning besides just making cards harder to get than others. A card's rarity determines how much of a card you're allowed to have in your deck. You can have 4 Copies of common cards, 3 copies of Uncommon cards, 2 copies of Rare cards, 1 copy of Epic cards, and 1 copy of Legendary cards. You can have as many of each rarity in your deck as you want, but each card can't exceed its rarity's limit."
