		"Icons and Costs",
		"Icons are how you play every card in the game. Without icons, you can't play the majority of your cards. At the beginning of the game, each players starts with 2 red, green, blue, and yellow icons, and 4 white icons. At the beginning of your turn, you gain 2 white icons. (The player that goes first does not gain 2 white icons on their first turn) Above the card image, every card has a cost shown as dots, or icons. You must pay icons equal to the displayed cost to activate a card. EXAMPLE: The Doge card has 1 white dot (icon) above its card image, meaning you only have to pay 1 white icon to summon the card, while Uncle Doge has 3 yellow dots and 2 white dots (icons) meaning you need to pay 3 yellow icons, and 2 white icons to summon the card. You may be wondering at this point, how do you gain icons besides white ones, which are earned at the beginning of your turn? Well, there's two ways, and they both involve the card's trait! (Color of the card image's background) During the end of your turn you gain an icon for every card of that icon's trait that's on the field. For example, let's say you have 3 Shamrock Doges on your field. Since all 3 of them have a yellow trait, at the end of your turn, you gain 3 yellow icons. The other way to gain icons is by discarding them. If you discard a card by right-clicking or down-swiping it, you gain 1 icon based on its trait. This should only be done if you really need icons. But don't be afraid to do this if need be!"
